From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 22:16:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] build: no LTO for packages compiled with trapping sanitizers

With -fsanitize-trap, a sanitizer's checks become trap instructions
instead of calls into its runtime; which form they take is decided
where GCC expands them. Under LTO that is the link, and lto-wrapper
passes no sanitizer option on from the objects: only the link line's
count. Many packages link with TARGET_LDFLAGS alone, as make's built-in
rule does, and libtool drops -fsanitize-trap from every link line it
runs. With CONFIG_TARGET_OPTIMIZATION holding -fsanitize=undefined
-fsanitize-trap=undefined, mtd and libnftnl, which ask for LTO, linked
their checks as calls into libubsan, which the musl toolchain does not
have.

Build without LTO when TARGET_CFLAGS asks for traps, whatever the
package asks for: each check is then expanded where the object is
compiled, with every flag. A build without trapping sanitizers is
unchanged.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 include/package.mk | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/package.mk b/include/package.mk
index f0e622a..c187ac0 100644
--- a/include/package.mk
+++ b/include/package.mk
@@ -54,11 +54,15 @@ ifeq ($(call pkg_build_flag,gc-sections,$(if $(CONFIG_USE_GC_SECTIONS),1,0)),1)
   TARGET_CXXFLAGS+= -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections
   TARGET_LDFLAGS+= -Wl,--gc-sections
 endif
+# Under LTO a sanitizer expands its checks at the link, with the link line's
+# options only, where -fsanitize-trap may be missing: expand them at compile time.
 ifeq ($(call pkg_build_flag,lto,$(if $(CONFIG_USE_LTO),1,0)),1)
+ifeq ($(filter -fsanitize-trap%,$(TARGET_CFLAGS)),)
   TARGET_CFLAGS+= -flto=1 -fno-fat-lto-objects
   TARGET_CXXFLAGS+= -flto=1 -fno-fat-lto-objects
   TARGET_LDFLAGS+= -flto=1 -fuse-linker-plugin
 endif
+endif
 ifdef CONFIG_USE_MOLD
   ifeq ($(call pkg_build_flag,mold,1),1)
     TARGET_LINKER:=mold
